WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.980
Trouble Soaring Through Heaven

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.980
Robïach Saisera

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:11.270
Jinto!

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.320
Are you okay?!

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.650
You look awful for a princess.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.740
You look just as bad.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.120
<i>I repeat.</i>

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.620
<i>We are in a state of emergency.</i>

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.830
<i>We apologize for the inconvenience,</i>

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.340
<i>but Guzornyu Fantasy Park...</i>

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.130
<i>...is closed due to an emergency.</i>

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.630
I guess we were right on.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.420
The cave's connected to a place like this?

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.550
<i>Please line up at the exit...</i>

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.680
What do they mean by emergency?

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.390
If it has nothing to do with us, then I've got no idea.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.600
In any case, we should hurry.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.230
Please stop right there.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.110
Please stop right there.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:58.990
You did not enter this park through a proper entrance.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:03.450
A security officer will be here to question you.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.330
Get out of the way.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.160
Please stop right there.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.620
You're not intelligent beings.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.040
No, we're not.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.380
But don't tell that to the children.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.590
It'll break their hearts.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.130
Jinto, we'll have to destroy them.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.630
But I don't feel good about it.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:20.680
Neither do I!

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.970
But they'll catch up to us unless we do something.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.930
This is a warning!

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:31.810
You have committed a crime of vandalism.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.110
We further require compensation for damages-

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.110
Then you better disappear before you're destroyed!

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.700
Sorry.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.990
Look at them. What an atrocious display.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.450
Move away from the trespassers!

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.290
Cancel clause 24 functions.

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.920
We must hurry, Inspector.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.880
Get the mechanical animals out of there.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.000
They'll just get in our way.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.710
I'd like to, but I can't.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.470
Something's jamming the transmission.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.970
This is the best we can do, since we're limited to voice commands.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.100
I'm sensing that you know more than you've told us?

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.220
I did receive orders.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:13.270
I've been told that as of 12:00, transmissions will be jammed.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:16.820
Communication will therefore be impossible during this time...

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.730
...so we're to just continue with our present orders.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.030
I want to know the reason for jamming the transmissions.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.070
I haven't got a clue.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:25.990
I see.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.200
I bet the Abh are back.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.370
The Abh are full of strange customs.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.290
The spaceship isn't too far away.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.090
We can see that with our own eyes.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:37.880
No.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.960
I'm talking about our own spaceship.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.300
Let's hurry.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:42.970
What is it?

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:45.970
It's as if...

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.220
...we're running through a maze.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.100
Let's ask him!

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.180
Good idea.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.690
Welcome, welcome.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.360
We'd like to know where the exit is.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.400
The exit?!

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.860
Are you leaving already? How sad!

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.160
The park is closed due to an emergency. Didn't you know?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.320
That can't be.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:09.660
The Guzornyu Fantasy Park is open 24 hours a day...

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.160
As I said, it's an emergency.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.910
Are you going to tell us or not?

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.420
I guess I'll have to.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.920
What the hell was that?!

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.210
To the men, or rather, the intruders who bombed the emergency exit.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.260
Please control yourselves while in the park!

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.880
Please refrain from destroying property!

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.680
Looks like your friends are here.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:28.890
Are you sure?

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:29.560
Hey, faster!

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.890
I can't go much faster, Inspector.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.480
The animals here don't understand the traffic rules.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.400
That's because these roads aren't for cars.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.820
We should've come in an aircraft!

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.820
Should I call for backup?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.570
Get real! We haven't got time!

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.870
Inspector! Over there!

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:49.530
Damn it!

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.540
All right! Get 'em!

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.580
Not here!

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.500
Stop where you are! This is the police!

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:04.170
I doubt there's a single person in this galaxy who would stop when told to stop.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.090
Officers, get outta the car!

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.470
Officers, prepare to fire!

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:10.890
After them!

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:12.720
Let me through!

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.640
Sorry!

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:16.440
Bad children!

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.520
Sorry.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:20.520
Can I point out one thing?

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.770
What?

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.780
We're heading back the way we came.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.530
We've got no other choice!

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.030
The enemy that was following us are there!

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.450
Did you forget?

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:36.000
You're divinely carefree.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.040
I'm impressed.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.830
Thank you.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.710
Well, I thought you were leaving.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.300
Are you back to buy something this time?

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.840
You have an aircraft or spaceship?

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.590
Of course!

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:51.800
Oh, no!

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.470
Lafiel, this way!

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.310
What?

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.640
Where are you going mister?!

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.100
I said stop!

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:04.320
There they are!

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.570
We must hurry.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.570
He's just one of many soldiers out to find us.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:12.660
He reported us.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.540
I know that!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.170
What's going on?!

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:40.810
Withdraw!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:42.560
What are you saying?!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.110
This is a battlefield.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.650
Entering here would be like some cocky brat mixing it up with professional fighters.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:52.610
This is no place for us cops!

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:54.620
Get moving!

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.540
Retreat to our cars!

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.410
But Inspector!

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.620
They're right in front of us!

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.170
We can't withdraw now!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.330
If you want to catch them that badly...

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.630
...go join your friends over there.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.470
Damn!

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.680
The mistake was coming here in the first place.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.560
Jinto, now! This way!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.150
Welcome! Welcome...!

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:25.730
Step back!

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:26.900
Welcome-

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.160
Damn!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.700
You okay?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.540
Of course I am.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.160
I'm kin of the stars.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:42.710
All right.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:54.890
Lafiel!

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.060
I'm ashamed to say that I'm very exhausted.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.730
Land's got double the gravity you're used to and we did run an awful lot.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:14.690
The Grand Chamberlain would have a fit if he ever saw me like this.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:16.700
Is he strict with manners?

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:17.490
Yes.

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:19.490
He always used to scold me.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.210
Actually, he probably wouldn't mind...

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:27.420
...since I carry myself with elegance whenever the time and place calls for it.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:28.750
I believe you.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:34.630
Unfortunately, I guess I've never been with you during any of those times.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:35.880
You shall watch your mouth.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.300
I'm always elegant.

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:39.010
Really?

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.970
Say anything else and I'll tear you to pieces.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.810
That could be a problem.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:49.770
We haven't got a chance in hell if they charged in right now.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:51.530
Let's go.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:56.030
I'll carry you on my back if you want.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:56.610
Fool.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:59.320
I wonder if she would've...

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:02.160
...put her arm around me like this when we first met.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:08.170
She would've told me to take the logbook and go on alone.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:10.590
I was happy for her reliance.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.300
Are you tired?

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:15.720
Very much.

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:19.430
You're awfully heavy for children.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.640
You sure you're not adults?

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:24.600
We have some problems with our obesity.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:29.020
It's my first time to carry two kids as big as you two at once.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:29.650
Sorry.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:30.980
I'm okay.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.690
Great. Then, can you go faster? To the exit.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:34.690
Of course.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:38.570
Jinto!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:42.740
They're coming!

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:46.660
You shall lean back!

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.210
Go faster!

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:52.920
Top left!

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:58.760
We can't go that way!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:08:59.760
It's a short cut!

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:03.930
Stay low!

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:07.430
There's no end to this.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:12.190
What are they doing? They're making it so much more difficult to run.

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:13.860
They're coming.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.360
They're copying us!

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:18.780
I'll leave them to you.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.120
I've got my hands full.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.950
But there's not much I can do.

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:27.500
Faster!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.920
Really? Sure, but tell me when it's unsafe.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.670
Here's the last one!

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:45.760
You shouldn't be littering on the streets!

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:47.980
I'm a very bad boy.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.640
There's the exit.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.110
Are you okay?

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.700
I'm not allowed to go any further.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.620
Thank you.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.500
There's more coming. We shall hurry!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.790
I know.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.790
Please come again.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.170
Sorry.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:21.380
Warning, warning.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:23.010
The gates are closing.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:25.100
Please step away from the gates.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:29.520
Warning, warning. The gates are closing.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.440
Please step away from the gates.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.400
Freeze!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.360
Don't do it!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.690
Why not? Are you going to just give up?

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:40.990
That's right.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.200
Look.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.070
They're the local police.

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:46.370
We'd be better off than being caught by the enemy.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:48.370
What if they hand us over?

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.040
We'll tackle that problem when we face it.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.410
If we fight here...

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:54.670
...we're guaranteed to die.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:59.630
I'm Inspector Entrnh of the Lune Vega City Police.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:04.260
I'd like to ask you a few questions regarding a car stolen 5 days ago.

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:06.390
Are you going to arrest us?

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.390
No. We ask that you come with us voluntarily.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:14.400
Although I should be able to arrest you on charges of property damage and unlawful use of a weapon.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:17.520
I claim legitimate self-defense.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:20.650
That's what I thought, so I didn't include the murders.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.610
However, it would be in your best interest to come with us.

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:26.910
At this rate, the occupying army will kill you.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:28.450
Lafiel...

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:31.910
I will trust your judgement.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:34.620
That's good.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:38.460
We won't need to use force as long as you cooperate.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.670
You're too easy on them, Inspector.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.800
United Mankind?!

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:43.550
You tricked us!

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:45.260
Wait, let me explain!

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.550
We're not collaborating with the occupying army!

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:49.140
I'm the officer in charge here.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.430
There's no problem as long as you do as I say.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:53.390
That's not quite true!

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:54.600
There is a problem.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.520
You didn't check whether they're completely unarmed!

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.150
How can you trust them?!

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:03.190
I swear, in the name of the Abh...

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:04.900
...I have no more weapons.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.610
Not good enough!

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:10.910
If you want me to believe you, take your clothes off and lie there on your back.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.290
I'll thoroughly check you out myself.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.620
That's enough.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.330
Hurry up and do as I say.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:22.500
You're a bunch of shameless beings with no morals.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.210
You disgusting synthetic humans.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:26.380
You filthy Abh!

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.930
That's enough!

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:32.350
Inspector, how old do you think I am?

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.480
Well, I'd say about 27, 28...

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.690
I'll be 49 this year.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.570
What?!

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.280
You're older than I am?!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.990
Oh, I see.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.950
You've gone through gene modification.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:53.040
Have you heard of the Silesia Republic?

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:54.830
No.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:13:00.130
They lost in a war about 120 years ago and became part of the United Mankind.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:03.050
Gene modification was practiced there.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:06.920
Well, it was more a practice of reversing the aging process.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:09.260
So you were a subject.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.350
It was my grandfather who actually received the treatment.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.640
That's three generations ago.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.560
It doesn't matter how long ago it was.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:19.900
My birth certificate states that I'm one of the immortal Silesians.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:23.360
So the organization sees you as an outcast, huh?

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.990
Then what makes you so zealous about your duties?

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.780
Go on! Take your clothes off!

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.580
That's out of the question!

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:36.160
Get outta the way!

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:38.290
You pathetic slave!

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:43.340
Jinto!!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.260
You bastard!

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.010
You will pay!

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.680
No. Don't, Lafiel...

00:13:58.810 --> 00:13:59.850
Who did that?!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:04.650
Hurry up! Get in!

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.700
Don't shoot! We'll hit each other!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:11.660
You shall me let go!

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:13.410
We haven't got time!

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:15.200
I'll kill him!

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:20.830
I'm going to turn the guy who did this to Jinto into space dust!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:21.750
Let go!

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:30.550
We're not in space, so the best you'll do is burn his corpse to a crisp.

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:32.380
We're ready, Bill!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:33.890
Here we go!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.690
What the hell was that?!

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:46.150
You useless piece of shit! Give me back my weapon!

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:50.530
I was sympathetic to you...

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.990
...but you've gone too far.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.360
We're going after them!

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:55.450
All officers in their cars!

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.460
What is it this time?!

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.500
Are you okay, Jinto?

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.710
It's just a scratch.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:12.010
Daswani, let's switch seats.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:13.430
Please treat his injury.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:16.100
How'd you know we'd be coming out from there?

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:18.680
If you had reached the main stream...

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.640
...it would've been difficult to find you since there are a number of exits.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:25.230
So we surrounded Fantasy Park in case you took that route and there you were.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:27.520
Would've been nicer if it was before I was shot.

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.070
You're lucky that we were there at all.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.440
Oh, by the way...

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:33.610
Isn't there something you'd like to tell us?

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.160
Like, for instance, a "thank you".

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.120
Or maybe a "thank you".

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.740
Or perhaps even a "thank you"?

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:43.080
A million thanks.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:46.500
But you're still planning on using us as hostages, right?

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.460
I told you before.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.420
We want a spaceship.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:54.470
But why go through all this danger?

00:15:54.470 --> 00:16:00.760
We realized after we split up just how incredibly valuable you are as hostages.

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.560
How stupid of me.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.690
I have a question for the Abh girl.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:06.480
What is it?

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:11.020
Are Abriel ears allowed by those outside the imperial family?

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:12.480
No.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.780
Well, I thought so.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.950
Can I ask you for your name...

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.080
...Your Highness?

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:24.410
Ablïarsec néïc Dubreuscr Bœrh Parhynr Lamhirh.

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:31.170
Do you know why I brought you here?

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.590
You have a crush on me?

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.130
You'll be my navigator...

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.220
...on our way to hell.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:43.180
Once I catch that Abh, I'll first kill you on the spot.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:47.140
Next, I'll kill the accomplices who interfered in the arrest...

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:51.230
...and then I'll get that pet boy of hers.

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:55.240
If the artificial mind of the Abh has even a hint of emotion...

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.860
...she might even mourn.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:59.240
Why are you doing this?

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:02.700
Because, I can't forgive them!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:07.790
I can't forgive them for always attaining happiness in the end!

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.960
You're jealous of them.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.460
Néïc Dubreuscr?

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.630
That's the name of the imperial family's first in line, isn't it?

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.380
We might get not only a spaceship...

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:19.090
...but independence itself.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.720
That decides it, Bill.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:22.220
To the funeral center!

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:26.930
But first, we should concentrate on getting rid of some pests.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:28.810
It's the police.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.940
Wouldn't it be wiser for you guys to just give up?

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.860
The police are after us.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:37.070
I don't want to involve you in this.

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:38.240
Fire!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.990
Those men are not from the police!

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:47.330
Leave it to me.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.750
I've disconnected all safety devices for a situation like this.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.250
Hold on tight!

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:54.630
Do you have anything, Min?

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:59.300
I've got a K211, of the former Caminteil Republic.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:03.550
It still has a reputation for the highest absorption rate anyway.

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:06.810
Here! You can have this!

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:09.310
And here's another!

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:10.940
What were those?

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:12.770
Sensor mines.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.190
Don't slow down!

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:19.860
It's just a smoke screen!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.120
Those were mines!

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:27.160
Our electromagnet is damaged.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:29.870
Stop the car!

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.080
Don't stop, you fool!

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:32.830
We've got cars behind us!

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:41.550
An accident.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:44.800
One should always be mindful of safe driving.

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:48.140
The frequency jamming is still in effect, isn't it?

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.560
Yes, it is.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.640
So they won't be able to call for help.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.650
But something's coming.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.400
Don't scare me. It's just the fire brigade.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.740
That's a fire, after all.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.530
Ah, the enemies were riding police cars, weren't they?

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:08.660
Yeah, so?

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.750
If they're seizing police cars...

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.250
...maybe they'll do the same with the fire department?

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.420
<i>Notice to citizens.</i>

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.170
<i>Cooperate with our search.</i>

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.340
<i>Politely answer all questions asked.</i>

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.340
See that flickering light?

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:24.640
That's a sign that we've taken over the Traffic Department.

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:29.560
All underground passages will be closed shortly and our soldiers will cover every inch of the city.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.890
The Abh have nowhere to run.

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:34.310
You're overdoing it.

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:38.190
I think we should split up from you here.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.570
I told you.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.320
You've already involved us enough.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.280
We can't just walk away, now that we've come this far.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.990
A spaceship or independence will not be possible...

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.870
...but I'm certain that the Crybh family will...

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.250
...reward you in some way for your help.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.250
We must have a spaceship.

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:57.500
I'm telling you, that's impossible.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:59.920
Can't you lend them one?

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:03.380
Yes, that might be possible.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:05.630
Then please promise me, Princess...

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.640
...that you will lend us a spaceship.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:11.930
I can only promise that I'll ask the Empress.

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.980
We'd appreciate that.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.600
If I survive long enough to see Her Majesty again...

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:19.270
...I will ask her.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:22.110
We'll make sure you survive this.

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:25.450
We have the ability to send you back to space.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.280
What do you mean?

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.660
The Undertaker...

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:29.830
...is an undertaker.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:37.500
I was wondering what these were when I first saw them.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.420
So, they're huge graves.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:43.380
Don't mistake a funeral center for a graveyard.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.170
That's an unforgivable mistake.

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:46.430
Uh, Sorry....

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:48.800
Then, what are they?

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:50.600
They're coffins.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.060
What?!

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:54.140
The graveyard's up there.

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:59.920
Man, it's scary to think how much today's kids are ignorant of basic customs.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.360
It's common sense, Jinto.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:06.400
Naturally, when someone dies, the corpse is released into space.

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:07.950
Wow.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.120
Huh? You don't think...?

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.120
We found them.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:14.120
It says here that they've found an Abh-like person.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.370
Have they been caught?

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.960
I'm going to catch them myself!

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:20.500
Hey, head to the northwestern district!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:23.500
Begin funeral preparations.

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:28.300
What is that?

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.890
I wonder. I'm not too familiar with this area.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.560
We can easily find out, you know.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:36.480
Then why don't you do that?

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:39.230
The Abh have nowhere to run.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:41.480
I'm going to get them.

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:44.270
Marca, they're here.

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:46.490
But nothing to worry about.

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:48.240
It's only the fire department.

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:51.410
We'll be ready to launch in about one minute.

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:53.280
What will you people do?

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:56.080
You look like you're feeling a lot better.

00:21:56.700 --> 00:21:58.370
We'll be okay.

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:00.040
This is where we were born and raised.

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:03.250
We're not about to be caught by some foreign idiots.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.960
As for you, the biggest danger is in the launch itself.

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:10.050
You've got no armor, so be careful.

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:11.720
Thanks.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:14.350
But I don't know how we can be careful.

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:16.180
We can't even steer it.

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:17.520
There's one way.

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:19.230
You can pray.

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:21.190
I don't believe it!

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:24.440
How could they think of escaping like that?!

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:27.150
Why didn't you tell me...

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:29.110
...about these Clasepyr funeral traditions?!

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:30.990
You never asked.

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:33.370
Where's our backup?!

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:35.080
They've just arrived!

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:36.540
How many?

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:37.410
Five aircraft.

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:39.040
Only five?!

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:42.040
They're asking us where they should land.

00:22:42.790 --> 00:22:44.960
Look out for one that's about to launch!

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:46.920
And destroy it immediately!

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:48.920
Got that?! lmmediately!

00:22:49.630 --> 00:22:52.010
Hurry! You're launching in 30 seconds!

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:55.140
So, don't forget about the spaceship.

00:22:55.680 --> 00:22:57.600
All right. I promise you.

00:22:59.430 --> 00:23:03.230
I never imagined I'd experience being a corpse while I'm alive.

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:04.480
Does it still hurt?

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:06.270
It's just a scratch.

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:09.490
This is humiliating...

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:13.910
...to have to ride a ship with no spatial sensors or gooheik.

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:15.820
This is not a ship.

00:23:15.820 --> 00:23:18.950
It's a coffin. C-O-F-F-I-N.

00:23:18.950 --> 00:23:20.620
It's cramped in here.

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:23.830
I suddenly have the urge to get away from you. Stay away.

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:27.500
Ouch! Be careful, I'm injured.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:29.130
I thought it was just a scratch.

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:32.470
Jinto.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:33.680
Yeah?

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:35.220
You shall forgive me.

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:36.100
For what?

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:39.180
You have-

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:42.940
Yeah.

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:47.820
Next time we get in one of these, we won't be talking to each other.

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:49.020
You fool.

00:23:49.020 --> 00:23:50.530
I'll tell you now.

00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:52.070
I've made a decision.

00:23:52.070 --> 00:23:53.110
Decision on what?

00:23:53.110 --> 00:23:55.780
That I'll remain by your side until the next time.

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:02.620
What are you waiting for?!

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:04.620
Why aren't you shooting?!

00:24:04.790 --> 00:24:06.750
Ram it!

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:08.920
Aim your aircraft at it!

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:10.420
Damn it!

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:12.590
Get assistance!

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:14.970
Where's the anti-aircraft unit!

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:18.430
Just shoot down that piece of trouble soaring into the sky!

00:24:22.270 --> 00:24:24.730
Damn it!

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:29.570
I won't allow them to get away like that!

00:24:29.570 --> 00:24:31.110
It's no use.

00:24:31.110 --> 00:24:35.320
That trouble soaring into the sky is trouble soaring to heaven.

00:24:37.280 --> 00:24:39.120
Trouble soaring to heaven!

00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:40.990
Now there's a good one!

00:24:42.490 --> 00:24:44.000
Why?!

00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:47.880
Why are they always the lucky ones?

00:24:48.790 --> 00:24:57.090
God will praise us but not grant us even the sacrifice of one person!

00:24:58.970 --> 00:25:02.770
That's all I'm asking to comfort my soul.

00:25:03.520 --> 00:25:07.020
Why is it?!

00:25:13.980 --> 00:25:16.360
Executive officer, I have an urgent message.

00:25:16.360 --> 00:25:17.110
Read it out.

00:25:17.110 --> 00:25:17.950
Aye-aye.

00:25:19.490 --> 00:25:20.490
Calling commander.

00:25:20.490 --> 00:25:21.950
What is it?

00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:26.460
We have word that a scout ship of the Lardbyrsh has rescued castaways drifting in orbit.

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:27.830
And?

00:25:27.830 --> 00:25:29.670
The castaways claim to be...

00:25:29.670 --> 00:25:33.550
...Bœrh Parhynr and His Excellency, Count Haïder.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.590
Is that so?

00:25:35.590 --> 00:25:45.640
She looks like that because Your Excellency dressed Her Highness in those rags, and dyed her hair black?

00:25:45.640 --> 00:25:47.100
Well...

00:25:47.100 --> 00:25:49.310
You see, I had no choice.

00:25:49.810 --> 00:25:52.860
No, no. That's beautiful, Count.

00:25:52.860 --> 00:25:55.190
I heard you were training to become a supply officer.

00:25:55.190 --> 00:25:58.400
I'd love to have you serve under me.

00:25:58.400 --> 00:25:59.150
Huh...

00:25:59.150 --> 00:26:00.700
Don't worry about it, Jinto.

00:26:00.700 --> 00:26:04.540
She's using you to make fun of me.

00:26:04.540 --> 00:26:06.200
Typical Spoor.

00:26:08.410 --> 00:26:12.500
Anyway, we must first treat the Count's injury.

00:26:12.500 --> 00:26:14.840
I'll have someone take you to the medical room.

00:26:14.840 --> 00:26:20.010
I'd love to hear about your adventures after that.

00:26:20.010 --> 00:26:24.220
In any case, I find it truly amazing.

00:26:24.220 --> 00:26:27.140
You dressing Her Highness like that, and yet...

00:26:27.140 --> 00:26:29.440
...you're forgiven with just a shot to the shoulder.

00:26:30.230 --> 00:26:32.020
I'm not the one who shot him!

00:26:33.020 --> 00:26:36.020
We then finally made it to the capital.

00:26:36.960 --> 00:26:41.740
And it was there that we learned of Gosroth's demise.

00:26:44.620 --> 00:26:47.290
Those were wonderful days.

00:26:47.290 --> 00:26:49.580
Plakia and I were truly in love with each other.

00:26:49.580 --> 00:26:54.420
We'd make use of our privilege to cause each other trouble.

00:26:54.420 --> 00:26:55.740
Privilege?

00:26:55.750 --> 00:26:57.460
Cause each other trouble?

00:26:57.460 --> 00:27:00.380
To be able to cause trouble to each other.

00:27:00.380 --> 00:27:02.260
I'm relieved, little child.

00:27:02.260 --> 00:27:05.140
Seems you're still too young to fall in love.

00:27:05.140 --> 00:27:06.970
Do you think so?

00:27:06.970 --> 00:27:13.440
Tell me, was it your idea to have me board Plakia's ship?

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:16.110
Too far-fetched to be a coincidence.

00:27:16.110 --> 00:27:20.820
I wanted her to refine the jewel that I brought up.

00:27:20.820 --> 00:27:23.450
Tell me one more thing.

00:27:23.450 --> 00:27:27.700
Do you know Plakia's evaluation of me?

00:27:28.120 --> 00:27:30.040
She told me simply...

00:27:31.290 --> 00:27:33.620
...that she was proud of you.

00:27:36.130 --> 00:27:37.460
Proud...

00:27:42.840 --> 00:27:46.470
What would your ancestors think if they saw an Abriel breaking down in tears.

00:27:46.470 --> 00:27:50.310
After having built a up a bad reputation for heartlessness.

00:27:51.140 --> 00:27:55.310
Those born to the Abriels do not have the right to cry.

00:27:55.310 --> 00:27:59.320
Don't even let anyone know.

00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:01.650
If you must cry...

00:28:01.650 --> 00:28:03.410
...do so where you're not seen.

00:28:03.650 --> 00:28:05.700
Father, that's not fair.

00:28:05.700 --> 00:28:06.620
What's not fair?

00:28:06.620 --> 00:28:11.660
You never taught me how to cry without showing tears like you do.

00:28:13.580 --> 00:28:19.380
I was told later that ties with my home planet had been completely severed.

00:28:19.380 --> 00:28:22.170
Strangely, I felt no sadness.

00:28:22.760 --> 00:28:23.590
I wonder why?

00:28:24.340 --> 00:28:29.680
Perhaps I had already lost my home planet back then.

00:28:30.720 --> 00:28:37.730
Shortly after, I received confirmation of the execution of the Count Haïder, my father.

00:28:38.310 --> 00:28:42.480
The Haïder Constellation had joined with the United Mankind...

00:28:42.480 --> 00:28:44.570
...to fight against the Empire...

00:28:44.820 --> 00:28:47.910
...under orders of their new leader, Teal Clint.

00:28:50.910 --> 00:28:52.410
I was looking for you.

00:28:53.040 --> 00:28:53.950
That cat...

00:28:54.460 --> 00:28:55.330
His name's Diaho.

00:28:56.030 --> 00:28:59.380
He's Zanelia's son. Zanelia is Holia's daughter.

00:28:59.710 --> 00:29:00.630
Then...

00:29:00.630 --> 00:29:03.090
...that makes you Diaho's aunt.

00:29:03.090 --> 00:29:03.880
Fool.

00:29:05.630 --> 00:29:09.970
Tomorrow's the day you start management school, right?

00:29:09.970 --> 00:29:10.970
Yeah.

00:29:10.970 --> 00:29:13.600
I'll be going to school for the next three years.

00:29:13.600 --> 00:29:15.270
I'm not looking forward to it.

00:29:15.270 --> 00:29:16.690
How about you?

00:29:16.690 --> 00:29:19.060
No decision yet on which ship I'll be on.

00:29:19.060 --> 00:29:19.980
Oh.

00:29:19.980 --> 00:29:22.610
Well, take it easy until then.

00:29:22.610 --> 00:29:25.320
Once that's decided, you'll be headed for battle, right?

00:29:25.320 --> 00:29:27.150
Right. Three years...

00:29:28.200 --> 00:29:31.280
So you'll be a supply officer in three years, right?

00:29:31.280 --> 00:29:33.160
If all goes well, that is.

00:29:33.700 --> 00:29:36.870
I'll likely be Deca-Commander in three years.

00:29:37.620 --> 00:29:39.750
Then I should get my own ship.

00:29:40.250 --> 00:29:45.210
It would be an attack ship or an escort ship, though I'm hoping for an attack ship.

00:29:45.760 --> 00:29:47.010
Right.

00:29:47.010 --> 00:29:51.350
An attack ship will need a supply officer to keep records.

00:29:51.350 --> 00:29:52.290
And...

00:29:52.720 --> 00:29:58.980
...it's customary with the Laburec for the captain to have some say in the ship's crew.

00:29:59.980 --> 00:30:02.400
It's not guaranteed...

00:30:02.400 --> 00:30:05.440
...but it's possible if both the captain and crew member want it.

00:30:05.650 --> 00:30:07.990
I ask the future Deca-Commander Abriel.

00:30:07.990 --> 00:30:12.070
Should you come across a Supply Officer Linn...

00:30:12.070 --> 00:30:17.330
...please invite me to serve under you as your secretary.

00:30:18.660 --> 00:30:19.540
Right.

00:30:19.540 --> 00:30:22.350
If you insist, I'll just have to accept you.

00:30:22.540 --> 00:30:26.670
It's pretty much a given that I'm going to be Deca-Commander in 3 years...

00:30:26.670 --> 00:30:28.550
...so the rest is up to you...

00:30:28.550 --> 00:30:31.180
...so study hard and achieve that rank of Supply Officer.

00:30:32.680 --> 00:30:36.060
Okay, I'll do my best, Lafiel.

00:30:36.060 --> 00:30:39.310
Well, I'll see you again at dinner, Jinto.

00:30:39.310 --> 00:30:41.440
I'll be busy until then.

00:30:41.440 --> 00:30:42.690
Hey, what about Diaho?

00:30:43.480 --> 00:30:45.900
He seems to like you.

00:30:45.900 --> 00:30:48.150
Why not keep him company?

00:30:48.150 --> 00:30:49.240
You're free, right?

00:30:50.240 --> 00:30:51.610
You're unreal.

00:30:53.370 --> 00:30:54.410
Lafiel.

00:30:54.740 --> 00:30:57.370
You're still a lousy liar.

00:30:57.370 --> 00:31:01.210
But I'm happy that I'll be by your side again.

00:31:01.920 --> 00:31:06.380
I'll be getting old. I only have half your life span.

00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:10.220
But I will be by your side as much as I can.

00:31:10.800 --> 00:31:13.090
Whether it be the day you first take the jade throne...

00:31:13.890 --> 00:31:14.680
...or...

00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:17.560
...it be the day you vanish in Planar Space...

00:31:18.390 --> 00:31:21.310
...I will be by your side.

00:31:21.810 --> 00:31:23.350
Those are my intentions.

00:31:23.900 --> 00:31:26.360
The future that I've chosen.

00:34:01.940 --> 00:34:08.690
Seikai no Monshou

00:34:01.940 --> 00:34:08.690
Crest of the Stars

00:34:10.320 --> 00:34:14.990
Three years later

00:34:15.870 --> 00:34:18.540
You're taking Futuune away from me?

00:34:19.080 --> 00:34:20.330
As you're aware,

00:34:20.330 --> 00:34:24.040
we lost many ships in battle 3 years ago.

00:34:20.500 --> 00:34:24.210
Patrol Ship

00:34:20.500 --> 00:34:24.210
Heirbyrsh

00:34:24.040 --> 00:34:25.840
Our forces are back to normal now.

00:34:26.500 --> 00:34:31.160
I'll have you command a fleet and assist Fleet Admiral Trife.

00:34:31.670 --> 00:34:32.930
You will start three days from now...

00:34:33.430 --> 00:34:35.100
...so prepare for a smooth transition.

00:34:35.800 --> 00:34:39.020
We'll talk about personnel for your new command later.

00:34:39.600 --> 00:34:41.270
Congratulations, Admiral Spoor.

00:34:42.230 --> 00:34:44.100
Congratulations?!

00:34:44.100 --> 00:34:47.730
Does he think I was hoping for a promotion or something?

00:34:47.730 --> 00:34:50.360
I'm already a Duchess.

00:34:50.780 --> 00:34:55.030
What are you looking so happy about, Chief of Staff?

00:34:55.030 --> 00:34:55.910
Uh, nothing.

00:34:55.910 --> 00:34:58.700
There's nothing wrong with being happy.

00:34:58.700 --> 00:35:01.080
You should also hurry with the transition.

00:35:01.290 --> 00:35:03.420
Huh? May I ask what for?!

00:35:03.420 --> 00:35:05.710
Because you are my new Chief of Staff.

00:35:05.710 --> 00:35:07.590
What?! Wait a minute!

00:35:08.130 --> 00:35:09.760
You're all promoted!

00:35:09.760 --> 00:35:11.010
I'm taking you with me!

00:35:14.090 --> 00:35:18.640
This isn't at all the space lifestyle I had in mind.

00:35:18.640 --> 00:35:19.970
There's nothing we can do.

00:35:20.220 --> 00:35:22.100
I left my dear husband and child...

00:35:22.100 --> 00:35:23.940
...to come to deep space...

00:35:22.230 --> 00:35:26.480
Light Transport

00:35:22.230 --> 00:35:26.480
Clasepyr

00:35:23.940 --> 00:35:27.310
...so why am I stuck shipping freight for the Empire?!

00:35:27.940 --> 00:35:29.150
There's nothing we can do.

00:35:29.150 --> 00:35:32.860
And it's not as if we're in control of the shipping.

00:35:33.070 --> 00:35:35.820
The operations of this ship are handled by an Abh.

00:35:35.820 --> 00:35:39.740
We haven't got much to do but drink booze...

00:35:39.740 --> 00:35:42.620
...and watch our bank accounts grow.

00:35:42.620 --> 00:35:44.370
There's nothing we can do.

00:35:44.750 --> 00:35:49.840
Hey, it's not so bad if you think we're saving up for...

00:35:49.840 --> 00:35:51.380
...the upcoming Clasepyr War for Independence.

00:35:51.380 --> 00:35:54.220
And we're doing it with the help of the Empire to boot.

00:35:54.220 --> 00:35:56.140
Yeah, pretty neat when you think about it.

00:35:56.140 --> 00:35:57.850
What's so neat about it?

00:35:57.850 --> 00:36:00.760
Let's just sit back and enjoy this until this war's over.

00:36:00.760 --> 00:36:02.980
Until it's over?

00:36:02.980 --> 00:36:05.730
It's hardly even begun.

00:36:05.730 --> 00:36:07.480
There's nothing we can do.

00:36:07.480 --> 00:36:10.190
Can't you say anything besides "There's nothing we can do"?

00:36:10.770 --> 00:36:14.150
Did I tell you about the guy who jumped into the thorn bush?

00:36:14.950 --> 00:36:16.910
Yeah, hundreds of times!

00:36:18.950 --> 00:36:21.870
Anti-matter Fuel Tank Inspection Ship

00:36:18.950 --> 00:36:21.870
Sernaic

00:36:21.610 --> 00:36:25.040
Wow. That was a close call.

00:36:25.040 --> 00:36:27.620
The magnetic density was dangerously low.

00:36:27.620 --> 00:36:34.550
However, the logic crystal to the remote observation had deteriorated to the point that...

00:36:34.550 --> 00:36:36.970
Your lies aren't going to get past me.

00:36:36.970 --> 00:36:38.550
You've done it again, Sernaic.

00:36:38.550 --> 00:36:39.680
She saw through me.

00:36:40.140 --> 00:36:43.930
Why repair a perfectly fine fuel tank?

00:36:43.930 --> 00:36:49.310
Because we can charge for repairs and make more...

00:36:49.310 --> 00:36:54.570
That's true, but there's more than enough work out there.

00:36:54.570 --> 00:36:57.400
And I'm sure the Bureau's starting to get suspicious.

00:36:57.400 --> 00:36:58.660
It's okay.

00:36:58.680 --> 00:37:01.990
We have the Crybh family backing us up.

00:37:01.990 --> 00:37:04.870
You shouldn't be relying on the royal family too much.

00:37:05.200 --> 00:37:06.160
Hey.

00:37:06.160 --> 00:37:08.920
Don't forget I'm the Chair of Sernaic and Company.

00:37:10.500 --> 00:37:13.670
Then can you make it without Grieda and myself?

00:37:13.670 --> 00:37:14.420
No.

00:37:14.420 --> 00:37:17.630
In that case, I'll pretend we didn't have this conversation.

00:37:17.630 --> 00:37:20.090
For this job, we'll just charge for the actual inspection.

00:37:20.430 --> 00:37:21.970
Come on!

00:37:23.180 --> 00:37:27.100
Attack Ship

00:37:23.180 --> 00:37:27.100
Basrogrh

00:37:36.490 --> 00:37:37.440
Captain.

00:37:37.440 --> 00:37:40.360
We're finished loading all food and supplies.

00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:45.870
There's only the two of us here, Jinto.

00:37:46.750 --> 00:37:47.960
Right.

00:37:47.960 --> 00:37:48.910
I really missed you.

00:37:49.620 --> 00:37:50.750
Listen.

00:37:50.750 --> 00:37:52.840
I'll let you in on a huge secret.

00:37:53.500 --> 00:37:54.880
I missed you too.

00:37:55.920 --> 00:37:57.340
Your secret is safe with me.

00:37:58.130 --> 00:38:02.890
It's been 3 years, yet you haven't changed one bit.

00:38:03.600 --> 00:38:06.220
I certainly hope I didn't change in a mere 3 years.

00:38:06.220 --> 00:38:07.850
You look older though.

00:38:08.770 --> 00:38:10.810
I'd rather you say I look more adult.

00:38:12.060 --> 00:38:14.520
I heard that chuckle, Captain.

00:38:14.520 --> 00:38:16.820
I told you, there's only the two of us here.

00:38:17.610 --> 00:38:21.570
Well, we can't act too friendly while others are around.

00:38:22.200 --> 00:38:22.990
Yeah.

00:38:22.990 --> 00:38:25.080
It isn't good for crew morale.

00:38:25.080 --> 00:38:27.040
In order that we don't unintentionally do it...

00:38:27.040 --> 00:38:32.960
...I should make a habit of calling you Captain, or Deca-Commander Abriel at all times.

00:38:33.750 --> 00:38:34.880
Is that what you want to call me?

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:37.840
Do you think that's what I want to call you?

00:38:39.260 --> 00:38:40.380
In that case...

00:38:41.130 --> 00:38:43.470
...you shall call me Lafiel!

00:38:46.470 --> 00:38:52.940
The beast drawn on this crest is an irregularly shaped...

00:38:52.940 --> 00:38:57.980
...eight-headed dragon called a Gaftonochec.

00:38:57.980 --> 00:39:09.830
This mythical beast was long forgotten until an empire had chosen it as their crest.

00:39:09.830 --> 00:39:16.250
The Gaftonochec then became the greatest beast among legendary creatures imagined by mankind.

00:39:16.250 --> 00:39:24.260
This was because this particular empire was the most powerful nation in the history of mankind.

00:39:24.260 --> 00:39:29.930
The race that built this nation is known as the Abh.

00:39:29.930 --> 00:39:33.770
Or perhaps they should be called the "kin of the stars"...

00:39:33.770 --> 00:39:39.480
...given that that's what they proudly proclaim themselves to be.

00:39:39.480 --> 00:39:46.570
In any case, let's limit our talk to the Gaftonochec...

00:39:46.570 --> 00:39:54.290
...since there is no limit to stories about the Abh race.

00:39:54.710 --> 00:39:59.590
"The Mythical Beast of Earth", by Roberto Lopez
